I come home to my flat.
It is very dark.
First, I screw the bulb into the lamp.
I turn it on.
Now there is light.
The lamp shines by the window.
Suddenly the flat is warm and alive.
It is not empty anymore.
Now I unpack my things.
I put the coffee in the cupboard.
I put the milk in the fridge.
The photo of my family stands on the table.
I stand for a moment in the soft light.
I look around my living room.
It is not just a temporary room.
For the first time, I really live here.
